==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|mūra}}, from {{etyl|la|de}} {{m|la|mūrus||wall}}. Related to {{cog|en|mure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaʊ̯ɐ/|/ˈmaʊ̯ər/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Mauer.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯ɐ|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Mauern|Mäuerchen}}

# a [[wall]], usually one made of [[stone]] or [[concrete]]

====Usage notes====
* See {{m|de|Wand}} for notes on the distinction between ''Mauer'' and this sometimes interchangeable word.

